nt and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[1668,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[716,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[1678,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[1656,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1519,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1661,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1652,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1712,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1654,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1662,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1665,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1708,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1520,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1658,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1655,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1653,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1663,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1551,"✅ Custom domains"],[1552,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1359,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1427,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1426,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1428,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[204,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1358,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[206,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1550,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1549,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1547,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1548,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[207,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[967,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[968,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[966,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[205,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[970,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1361,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1430,"❌ For more than 5